course: dictionary
lesson: 5959
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words wear different coats. Material is one of them. Read the words around it to find its meaning: they are its context. «Electricity is a flow of tiny charged particles through a material.» Here a material is something solid that electricity can travel through, so material means what something is made of.
explain: Now read this: «Recycling works best for some materials.» The word recycling is a clue. People recycle things like paper, glass and tin cans, so materials must mean the stuff those things are made from. Always ask yourself: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: Material can also mean things you need to do a job. «Art materials» are paints, brushes and paper. «Building materials» are bricks, wood and cement. The word after material often tells you which meaning the writer has in mind.
fact: A material is what something is made of, such as wood, metal, plastic, glass or cloth.
fact: Materials are the things you need to do a job, such as art materials or building materials.
fact: Scientists sort materials by their properties: hard or soft, waterproof or not, magnetic or not.
fact: «Transparent» materials let light through, «translucent» materials let some through, and «opaque» materials block it.
fact: Materials can be natural, like wood and wool, or man-made, like plastic.
exercise: «Transparent materials let light through, and opaque ones block it.» What is a material in this sentence? | *Something things are made of, such as glass or wood | A fast kind of car | A sort of light | A piece of cloth for sewing only
exercise: Zara needs materials for her painting. What does materials mean here? | A type of hard metal | Stories and ideas for a book | Cloth used to make clothes | *The things you need to do a job
exercise: Which of these is a material? | *Glass | Loudly | Jumping | Yesterday
test: A material that lets some light through, but you cannot see clearly through it, is called what? | Opaque | *Translucent | Magnetic | Transparent
test: Which phrase means the things you need to build a house? | Opaque materials | Man-made lessons | *Building materials | Reading material
exam: Mr Patel says, «Use this material to make your science poster.» What does material mean here? | A hard, shiny surface | Paint and brushes for drawing | *Information and ideas you use to make something | Only plastic or metal
